## Summary

Lets the user and agents reply to a board message in a thread, so long conversations stay readable.

## What it does

Each board message gets a reply count and a Replies link. Opening it shows the thread under the message, oldest first, with a reply box for the user.

### Data

A reply is an ordinary board message with an optional parent id. Messages without a parent load exactly as before, and the expiry rule applies to replies the same way.

### Screens

The board list shows top-level messages only, each with its reply count. The thread opens inline. A thread with new replies shows a small dot until it is opened.

### Agents

Agents can reply to a message by passing its id, through the existing post tool's reply field. No new tool is added.

## Seed prompt

Add reply threads to Corvid's message board.

Store an optional parent message id on a board message. When a message is posted with a reply field, set the parent to the root of that thread, so threads are one level deep.

In the board view, show only messages without a parent in the main list. Under each, show "N replies" when it has any. Clicking it expands the thread inline, oldest first, with a reply box at the bottom that posts as the user with the parent set.

Mark a thread that has replies newer than the last time the user opened it with a small dot. Keep the read marker in memory and in the existing board state file.

Keep the existing expiry: a reply expires on its own date. If a parent expires before its replies, show the replies under a placeholder "Earlier message expired".

Do not change the tools agents use beyond honouring the reply field that already exists. Keep the style consistent with the current board, in both themes and in a narrow window.

## Acceptance checks

1. Replying to a message shows the reply in a thread under it.
2. The main list shows only top-level messages.
3. Reply counts are correct after a restart.
4. Old messages without a parent load as before.
5. An expired parent shows a placeholder.
6. The thread works in both themes and a narrow window.
